I added consent.cancelled to both cancellation paths:

    cancellation by an authenticated organization user;

    cancellation by the signer through the public consent page.

The status change and audit event are saved in the same database transaction, so they cannot become inconsistent. The public cancellation records the signer source, IP address, and device details internally in the protected audit trail—not in the PDF. The changes preserve the existing creation and completion audit logic in both controllers.
